 "notes": "Count under way; no winner called. Lead change: Flávio led by 278,020 (34.1% counted), 12,941 (46.5%); Lula took the lead by 190,928 at 51.4% and widened it to 356,731 at 53.9% as Nordeste votes (BA 33%, PE 53%, CE 55%, PI 35% counted) arrive. Big Flávio areas still pending: SP 31%, RJ 9%, MG 48%, GO 60%. Extension: STF Justice Zanin granted a request from Lula's coalition (Reclamação 101673, over transit cuts in Salvador, Feira de Santana and Lauro de Freitas) and extended voting two hours nationally; he later clarified it applied only where machines were still open at 17h (TSE note, BBC). AP reports the decision came three minutes before polls closed, reached some stations after they had already shut, paused results until 19h, and sets the stage for possible legal challenges whoever wins. Flávio's campaign had asked for more time in rain-hit towns (G1). Bolsonaro allies called it an intervention that 'only helps whoever is losing' (Guardian); no published vote-impact analysis found.",
